  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many more acorns each squirrel needs to collect, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of acorns each squirrel needs to get through the winter.\n2. Determine how many more acorns each squirrel needs to collect by subtracting the number of acorns already collected from the total number of acorns needed.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the total number of acorns each squirrel needs.\nEach squirrel needs 130 acorns to get through the winter. Since there are 5 squirrels, the total number of acorns needed is:\n\\[ 130 \\times 5 = 650 \\]\n\nStep 2: Determine how many more acorns each squirrel needs to collect.\nThe squirrels have already collected 575 acorns. To find out how many more acorns each squirrel needs, we subtract the number of acorns already collected from the total number of acorns needed:\n\\[ 650 - 575 = 75 \\]\n\nTherefore, each squirrel needs to collect \\(\\boxed{75}\\) more acorns.",
